---
import { routingTiers } from "../../data/how-i-work";
---
<div class="how-routing" aria-label="Model routing by task complexity">
  <div class="how-routing__header">
    <span>routing policy</span>
    <p>Choose the route for the task's risk and reasoning load, then promote it when evidence reveals hidden coupling or external effects.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="how-routing__rows">
    {routingTiers.map((tier) => (
      <article>
        <span class="how-routing__tier">{tier.tier}</span>
        <div><strong>{tier.fit}</strong><small>{tier.work}</small></div>
        <p>{tier.evidence}</p>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="how-routing__note">The labels describe a portable policy, not a permanent provider ranking. Fresh context matters more to independent review than asking the same model to repeat the same assumptions.</p>
</div>
